      "scriptedTurns": [
        {
          "id": "turn-01",
          "thinkingMs": 2600,
          "thinkingLabel": "Drafting three intro emails…",
          "reply": [
            {
              "id": "turn-01-emails",
              "type": "email_drafts",
              "text": "Here are three intro emails, one per contact — each written to their role in the deal. Review the reasoning on any card, or tell me what to change.",
              "emails": [
                {
                  "prospect": "Zack Turner",
                  "role": "VP, IT",
                  "company": "Cirrus",
                  "step": {
                    "type": "email",
                    "subject": "Backing Robert’s Hunter evaluation",
                    "body": "Hi Zack,<br><br>Your team is already looking at Hunter with Robert — <span class='email-highlight' data-link='context' data-popover-title='Deal Context' data-popover-question='Is this the right thing to open on?' data-popover-body='Technical evaluation underway on the IT side; Robert (Director, IT) is the active contact.' data-source-label='Salesforce' data-source-icon='/assets/images/source_icons/source_salesforce.svg'>the technical evaluation is already underway on the IT side</span>. I wanted to reach you directly, since <span class='email-highlight' data-link='pain' data-popover-title='Buying Role' data-popover-question='Is this a fair read of his role?' data-popover-body='VP of IT — Robert’s manager and the budget owner for infrastructure decisions at Cirrus.' data-source-label='ZoomInfo' data-source-icon='/assets/images/source_icons/source_zoominfo.svg'>infrastructure decisions at this scale land on your desk</span>.<br><br>The short version: we consolidate enrichment across 15 data vendors into one workflow, inside the CRM your reps already use — nothing new for IT to stand up or secure.<br><br>Fifteen minutes to give you the executive view before Robert brings you the detail?",
                    "details": [
                      {
                        "title": "Email Type",
                        "value": "Warm intro — executive"
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Reasoning",
                        "value": "Reaches the budget owner above the technical contact so the deal keeps executive air cover if Robert’s priorities shift. The ask is a fifteen-minute exec briefing, not a demo — the version a VP takes from a stranger."
                      }
                    ],
                    "sources": [
                      {
                        "label": "Salesforce",
                        "icon": "/assets/images/source_icons/source_salesforce.svg"
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "ZoomInfo",
                        "icon": "/assets/images/source_icons/source_zoominfo.svg"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "prospect": "Monica Reyes",
                  "role": "Sr. Director, Data Architecture",
                  "company": "Cirrus",
                  "step": {
                    "type": "email",
                    "subject": "How Hunter fits your data model",
                    "body": "Hi Monica,<br><br>We’re partway into an evaluation with Robert’s team, and a deployment at your scale eventually runs through <span class='email-highlight' data-link='context' data-popover-title='Ownership' data-popover-question='Is this the right hook for her?' data-popover-body='Sr. Director, Data Architecture — owns the data model the integration plugs into. Her sign-off de-risks the technical evaluation.' data-source-label='Salesforce' data-source-icon='/assets/images/source_icons/source_salesforce.svg'>the account’s data architecture</span> — which is your call, not IT’s.<br><br>Hunter writes enriched records into your existing objects: <span class='email-highlight' data-link='solution' data-popover-title='Value Prop' data-popover-question='Is this the reassurance an architect wants first?' data-popover-body='No net-new schema and no shadow data store — enrichment lands on the objects already in the model.' data-source-label='G2' data-source-icon='/assets/images/source_icons/source_g2.svg'>no net-new schema, no shadow data store</span>. Most architects want to see exactly that before they sign off.<br><br>Worth a short session to walk your team through it, so the review doesn’t stall later?",
                    "details": [
                      {
                        "title": "Email Type",
                        "value": "Technical intro"
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Reasoning",
                        "value": "Engages the sign-off owner who isn’t in the deal yet, and leads with the first question a data architect asks — what it does to the schema. Pre-empts the review that most often stalls a technical evaluation."
                      }
                    ],
                    "sources": [
                      {
                        "label": "Salesforce",
                        "icon": "/assets/images/source_icons/source_salesforce.svg"
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "G2",
                        "icon": "/assets/images/source_icons/source_g2.svg"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "prospect": "Patrick O’Brien",
                  "role": "Manager, DevOps",
                  "company": "Cirrus",
                  "step": {
                    "type": "email",
                    "subject": "Rollout, from the team who’d run it",
                    "body": "Hi Patrick,<br><br>You’d likely own the day-to-day rollout if Cirrus moves forward with Hunter — <span class='email-highlight' data-link='context' data-popover-title='Working-Level Owner' data-popover-question='Is this why he belongs on the thread?' data-popover-body='Manager, DevOps — reports to Robert and would own day-to-day rollout. A friendly voice at the working level keeps momentum between the exec conversations.' data-source-label='ZoomInfo' data-source-icon='/assets/images/source_icons/source_zoominfo.svg'>so I’d rather you hear it from us early than inherit it later</span>.<br><br><span class='email-highlight' data-link='solution' data-popover-title='Setup' data-popover-question='Is this the operational detail he cares about?' data-popover-body='Median package install and field mapping time across 2025 Salesforce onboardings.' data-source-label='Salesforce' data-source-icon='/assets/images/source_icons/source_salesforce.svg'>Setup is a 30-minute package install and field mapping</span>, and there’s no new interface for your team to maintain — it lives in the CRM you already run.<br><br>Happy to walk through the deployment steps whenever it’s useful.",
                    "details": [
                      {
                        "title": "Email Type",
                        "value": "Working-level intro"
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Reasoning",
                        "value": "Opens a friendly line at the level that owns execution, so momentum holds between the executive conversations. Leads with the operational facts a DevOps manager weighs — setup time and maintenance surface — rather than the pitch."
                      }
                    ],
                    "sources": [
                      {
                        "label": "ZoomInfo",
                        "icon": "/assets/images/source_icons/source_zoominfo.svg"
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Salesforce",
                        "icon": "/assets/images/source_icons/source_salesforce.svg"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                }
